        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="113.710483185841" YPOS="1697.89255384615" OwnPage="2" ItemID="221863712" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="284.916814159292" HEIGHT="66.8083311096025" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="1" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L284.917 0 L284.917 66.8083 L0 66.8083 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L284.916 0 L284.916 66.8079 L0 66.8079 L0 0 Z" gXpos="113.710483185841" gYpos="865.88615384615" gWidth="282.55" gHeight="45.4146798798563" ALIGN="1" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle ALIGN="1" LINESP="28" FONT="Special Elite Regular" FONTSIZE="33" SCALEH="90" KERN="-10"/>
                <ITEXT SCALEH="90" KERN="-10" CH="Student Tells All: Internship at Anduril"/>
                <trail/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="114.4782" YPOS="1762.46870088496" OwnPage="2" ItemID="221877872" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="284.957946902655" HEIGHT="453.289699115039" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="2" COLGAP="7.2" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L284.958 0 L284.958 453.29 L0 453.29 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L284.958 0 L284.958 453.29 L0 453.29 L0 0 Z" gXpos="114.4782" gYpos="930.465500884942" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" PSTYLE="Default Paragraph Style" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle PARENT="Default Paragraph Style" LINESP="10" FONT="Bell MT Regular" FONTSIZE="9" KERN="0" LANGUAGE="en_US"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Bell MT Bold" FONTSIZE="9" CH="Camilia Creutzfeldt"/>
                <para PARENT="Default Paragraph Style" ALIGN="1" LINESP="10"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Bell MT Italic" FONTSIZE="9" KERN="0" CH="ECE @ CMU "/>
                <para PARENT="Default Paragraph Style" ALIGN="1" LINESP="10"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Bell MT Italic" FONTSIZE="9" KERN="0" CH="Systems Safety Intern @ Anduril "/>
                <para PARENT="Default Paragraph Style" ALIGN="1" LINESP="10"/>
                <para PARENT="Default Paragraph Style" ALIGN="1" LINESP="10"/>
                <ITEXT CH="    With fall break on the horizon, it's safe to say that we've fully settled into the semester. Yet, I still get people bringing up my summer internship at Anduril. That was two whole months ago! Most often, the people who bring it up are just classmates who want to find out more about what a chill time a chill guy like me had at a chill engineering firm. Once in a while, though, someone seems to take issue with me having interned at Anduril, talking about how it's &quot;unethical&quot; and that I &quot;kill&quot; people or whatever. So, let's set the record straight."/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    First of all, what I did that summer was entirely ethical. I deployed an internal dashboard for coordinating distributed nodes to help ensure synergy inside Anduril's product ecosystem. In layman’s terms, I made sure the drones arrived on time. If you imagine that each drone is a pointer, then anyone who’s written a linked list in 15-122: Principles of Imperative Computation has basically done the same thing I did. You might be asking, what do these drones do? That's an excellent question! The problem is, I don't actually know what the drone products my tool interacts with are specifically used for, but the applications of Anduril's unmanned aerial vehicles are practically endless: they could be used for removing unwanted elements from our operational spaces, payload delivery at supersonic timescales, and acute-onset hospital demolition."/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    Secondly, not only was what I did ethical, but Anduril as a whole is a fully ethical company. I don't know when it happened, but &quot;drones&quot; has become such a buzzword. Any old drone company is being labeled as unethical! I don’t see anyone protesting drones used to film weddings from above! Let me be clear: Anduril does not kill people, people kill people. The United States military uses Anduril's drones and systems to defend this country, and they just happen to incur a handful of collateral noncombatant casualties along the way! Palmer Luckey's hands are clean, and so are mine."/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    Lastly, if you still think what I'm doing is wrong, I'm afraid to tell you that you have just fallen victim to the is-ought fallacy. Just because what I'm doing ought to be illegal, doesn't mean it really is. They teach you about this in 76-101: Interpretation and Argument. But, of course, you wouldn’t know that."/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    Honestly, it's weird that people are antagonizing me over my attempt at career development. When students attend CMU, they do so with the expectation of getting an engineering job in SoCal. It is my right as a student of CIT to get a six-figure job right out the door. I'm done arguing whether or not my work is ethical: it obviously is, and my continued dwelling on the past isn't going to do me any favors. This is why I am proud to announce that next summer, I will be getting closer to the action by joining the Central Intelligence Agency as a destabilization strategy intern."/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="-194.4978" YPOS="2058.49255384615" OwnPage="-1" ItemID="227484080" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="281.464" HEIGHT="91.1371948264162" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="1" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L281.464 0 L281.464 91.1372 L0 91.1372 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L281.464 0 L281.464 91.1367 L0 91.1367 L0 0 Z" gXpos="-194.4978" gYpos="1226.48615384615" gWidth="282.55" gHeight="45.4146798798563" ALIGN="1" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle ALIGN="1" LINESP="28" FONT="Special Elite Regular" FONTSIZE="33" SCALEH="90" KERN="-10"/>
                <ITEXT SCALEH="90" KERN="-10" CH="Religious Proclamation of Gun-Fearing Disciples"/>
                <trail/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="745.066371681416" YPOS="1154.3824" OwnPage="-1" ItemID="227486912" PTYPE="6" WIDTH="208.007828318584" HEIGHT="14.976" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="1" PWIDTH="1" PCOLOR2="Black" PLINEART="1" path="M0 0 L208.008 0 L208.008 14.976 L0 14.976 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L208.008 0 L208.008 14.976 L0 14.976 L0 0 Z" gXpos="745.066371681416" gYpos="1154.3824" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0"/>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="-254.1938" YPOS="2181.4512" OwnPage="-1" ItemID="227475584" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="287.464" HEIGHT="195.810421238938" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="2" COLGAP="7.2" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L287.464 0 L287.464 195.81 L0 195.81 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L287.464 0 L287.464 195.81 L0 195.81 L0 0 Z" gXpos="-254.1938" gYpos="1349.44799999999" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" PSTYLE="Default Paragraph Style" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle PARENT="Default Paragraph Style" LINESP="10" FONT="Bell MT Regular" FONTSIZE="9" KERN="0" LANGUAGE="en_US"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Bell MT Bold" FONTSIZE="9" CH="joehill's Shoes"/>
                <para PARENT="Default Paragraph Style" ALIGN="1" LINESP="10"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Bell MT Italic" FONTSIZE="9" KERN="0" CH="Former Unitarian, redeemed Pythagorean "/>
                <para PARENT="Default Paragraph Style" ALIGN="1" LINESP="10"/>
                <para PARENT="Default Paragraph Style" ALIGN="1" LINESP="10"/>
                <ITEXT CH="    On the 250th anniversary of this nation, and the 2026th anniversary of the Christians’ God, my so-called unalienable right to freedom of religion has been, regrettably, alienated."/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    CMU has deemed my ceremonial bazooka “inappropriate for a safe campus environment”, despite it meeting the ATF’s 51” limit. Carrying this sacrosanct item is a foundational part of my religion’s canon, and mine was passed down from my grandfather who used it to baptize the atheist, Lenin-fearing Soviets in 1939. "/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    I acknowledge the Student Affairs’ efforts for a harmonious community here at CMU considering the diverse range of faiths. I simply plead this effort be extended to mine. I solemnly believe, at the end of the day, we are all trying to worship the same high-power force in our own ways."/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    If you have ever faced persecution or an incredibly minor inconvenience for your religious convictions, I implore you to speak up. Truly, my bazooka is purely ceremonious and mostly non-functional. Besides, with the CMUPD’s pepper spray and water-cannons, who is this rule actually “protecting”, anyway? "/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
